// Instrumentation.xcconfig — COMMITTED base configuration (contains NO secrets).
//
// This file is the target's base xcconfig. It declares the instrumentation
// build settings with EMPTY defaults, then optionally pulls in a gitignored
// secrets file that overrides them with the Owner's real values.
//
// Why a committed base + optional include (instead of referencing the gitignored
// file directly): a fresh checkout has no Secrets.xcconfig, and a build must
// still succeed with the SDKs dormant. Empty defaults here guarantee that; the
// `#include?` (optional include — no error when the file is absent) lets a
// developer/CI drop real values in without ever committing them.
//
// Precedence: values in the included Secrets.xcconfig REPLACE the empty defaults
// below. Info.plist surfaces these as EBPostHogAPIKey / EBPostHogHost /
// EBSentryDSN, which the app reads at runtime. An empty value == not configured
// == the SDK never initializes (fail-soft). See README "Instrumentation".

// ---- Empty defaults (dormant / fail-soft) ---------------------------------
POSTHOG_API_KEY =
POSTHOG_HOST =
SENTRY_DSN =

// ---- Owner secrets (gitignored; optional) ---------------------------------
// Copy Config/Secrets.xcconfig.example to Config/Secrets.xcconfig and fill in
// the real values out of band. That file is .gitignore'd and must never be
// committed.
#include? "Secrets.xcconfig"
